{% comment %}
  One heading element for a desktop text + an optional phone text (SEO tools read every <h*> in the HTML, so two
  tags per section showed up as duplicate headings).
  - Same words (only spaces / line breaks differ): the text once; the phone text's line breaks show on phones only
    (each break keeps a space before it, so desktop reads "Routine, Built", not "Routine,Built").
  - Different words: both texts inside the one tag, each hidden on the other screen size.
  Accepts: heading, heading_mobile, tag ('h1'|'h2'|'h3', default h2), class (on the tag). Output is escaped;
  [customers] → Theme settings → Customer count; "Money-Back" kept on one line.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign ht_tag = tag | default: 'h2'
  assign ht_d = heading | escape | replace: '[customers]', settings.customer_count | replace: 'Money-Back', '<span class="zenith-nowrap">Money-Back</span>' | replace: 'Money-back', '<span class="zenith-nowrap">Money-back</span>'
  assign ht_m = heading_mobile | escape | replace: '[customers]', settings.customer_count | replace: 'Money-Back', '<span class="zenith-nowrap">Money-Back</span>' | replace: 'Money-back', '<span class="zenith-nowrap">Money-back</span>'
  assign ht_dn = heading | strip_newlines | replace: ' ', '' | downcase
  assign ht_mn = heading_mobile | strip_newlines | replace: ' ', '' | downcase
-%}
{%- if heading_mobile == blank -%}
  <{{ ht_tag }} class="{{ class }}">{{ ht_d }}</{{ ht_tag }}>
{%- elsif heading == blank -%}
  <{{ ht_tag }} class="{{ class }} zenith-hide-desktop">{{ ht_m | newline_to_br | strip_newlines }}</{{ ht_tag }}>
{%- elsif ht_dn == ht_mn -%}
  <{{ ht_tag }} class="{{ class }}">{{ ht_m | newline_to_br | strip_newlines | replace: '<br />', ' <br class="zenith-hide-desktop">' }}</{{ ht_tag }}>
{%- else -%}
  <{{ ht_tag }} class="{{ class }}"><span class="zenith-hide-mobile">{{ ht_d }}</span><span class="zenith-hide-desktop">{{ ht_m | newline_to_br | strip_newlines }}</span></{{ ht_tag }}>
{%- endif -%}
